{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>In booths you shall dwell seven days.</b> I know only days; from where [do I know] nights? I apply a verbal analogy: it says here 'תשבו' and it says elsewhere 'in the Tent of Meeting תשבו' — just as 'תשבו' said regarding the Tent of Meeting makes its nights like its days, so too 'תשבו' said here, etc. And the Sages say: 'the fifteenth' is stated regarding the Festival of Matzot and 'the fifteenth' is stated regarding the Festival of Sukkot — just as there, the first night is obligatory and from then on optional, so too here. <b>In booths you shall dwell seven days.</b> Corresponding to the clouds of glory." "<b>All the citizen in Israel shall dwell in booths.</b> The convert does not need to be warned, for he has no other house; but the citizens and the settled residents in Israel, even though they have houses and great palaces, shall dwell in booths. This festival was fixed at the time of gathering the threshing floor and the winepress, lest their hearts grow proud over their houses, which are full of every good thing, and they say 'our hands made all this wealth for us.' Through dwelling in a booth they will give praise and thanksgiving to the One who gave them an inheritance and houses full of every good thing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:50.657383197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}